<title>USA: U.S. Senate defeats ethyanol tax.</title>
<headline>U.S. Senate defeats ethyanol tax.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Senate on Wednesday defeated a proposal to increase the federal fuel tax on ethyanol by three cents a gallon to help pay for anti-smoking programs.</p>
<p>Senators rejected the amendment, 76-24.</p>
<p>Sen. Jesse Helms, North Carolina Republican, proposed the amendment in a tit-for-tat move against midwestern senators who wanted to deny crop insurance to tobacco growers and to place an assessment on raw tobacco sales to pay for I.D. checks of youthful smokers.</p>
</text>
